# {{name}}

{{premise}}

An idle game on the watchpot engine ({{engine}}), scaffolded from its game template. Core: {{core}}. Features:
{{features}}. Built for {{session}}.

Needs Bun 1.4.3 or later (`bun check` typechecks).

## Commands

```sh
bun install
bun run dev        # http://localhost:3000 (PORT=<n> for another); #dev opens the dev panel
bun run verify     # typecheck, lint, the tests a change touches (every test before the first commit), the Decimal check
bun run gates      # typecheck, lint, every fast test, the build; gates:full adds the slow tier and the contract
bun run sim -- --contract     # four played hours on the auto-player, judged against the pacing bands
bun run sim -- --sessions     # a week of a person coming and going, never judged
bun run tokens     # after editing design/tokens.json
bun run lint:fix   # format
```

## Where things are

- `src/content/` the data: the words (`words.ts`), the economy, the core's list and one file per feature;
  `pacing.ts` holds how the sim plays and the pacing contract.
- `src/game/` the features on the engine's factories (`wallet`, `stats`, `settings`, the core and the chosen
  features), `income.ts`, `bus.ts`, `game.ts` (`defineGame`, the feature order and the save) and the store.
- `src/app/` the page: `App.tsx` over the `Shell`, the tabs, the header, the about sheet, the icons, the sounds, and
  `hooks.ts` (`useGameState`, `useGameView`, `useGameStore`). `src/screens/` one screen per tab.
- `src/ui/` the game's own components over the engine's headless `watchpot/ui`, each with its CSS module, and
  `theme.css`; `src/ui/README.md` lists the `--ui-*` tokens they read.
- `src/shaders/` the backdrop's fragment and its still.
- `design/tokens.json` the palette and type, compiled to `src/tokens.css` by `bun run tokens` (commit both).
- `sim/` the headless sim (`run.ts`) and what it reads off a row (`row.ts`). `test/` the game's tests.

The engine's guide is its `README.md` and `docs/` (`node_modules/watchpot/`). To move to a newer engine, change the
tag on `watchpot` in `package.json` and run `bun install`.

`.claude/` holds the concept as the scaffold took it down (`specs/concept.md`, the answers beside it) and notes for
an agent working on the game (`CLAUDE.md`); the game does not need them.
